{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011zPwgbnz4aHRx9ciKaUcni","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Property Manager MVP - Implementation Plan\n     2→\n     3→## Context\n     4→\n     5→Building a self-hosted, multi-user property management app. Landlords manage properties, units, leases, and billing; tenants can be linked to user accounts for future portal access. The project scaffolding (S01) and database schema (S02) are complete. We need to implement: authentication (S03), REST API (S04), properties + units CRUD (S05-S06), tenants + leases (S07-S08), and billing (S09, S11).\n     6→\n     7→The codebase already has: Next.js 14 App Router, Prisma schema (11 models), 23 shadcn/ui components, React Hook Form + Zod v4, NextAuth v5 beta, bcryptjs, date-fns, decimal.js, and Docker setup.\n     8→\n     9→---\n    10→\n    11→## Architecture Decisions\n    12→\n    13→- **Server Actions** for form mutations — colocated with forms, less boilerplate. Shared business logic lives in `/src/lib/services/` so both server actions and API routes can reuse it\n    14→- **REST API** (`/api/v1/...`) for external integrations — API key auth for service-to-service calls, supports webhooks (e.g., payment providers) and automation\n    15→- **DB session strategy** (`strategy: \"database\"`) — supports instant session revocation (critical for multi-user: landlord disables tenant, password changes, etc.), ability to list/manage active sessions, and no token-size bloat. Requires `Session` + `Account` models in Prisma\n    16→- **Route groups**: `(auth)` for login, `(dashboard)` for all protected pages with shared sidebar layout\n    17→- **Validation schemas**: `/src/lib/validations/` — one file per entity, shared between client, server actions, and API routes\n    18→- **Server actions**: `/src/lib/actions/` — one file per entity, all prefixed with `\"use server\"`\n    19→- **Service layer**: `/src/lib/services/` — one file per entity, pure business logic (no auth checks), called by both server actions and API routes\n    20→\n    21→---\n    22→\n    23→## Phase 1: Auth (S03)\n    24→\n    25→**Files to create:**\n    26→- `src/lib/auth.ts` — NextAuth config: CredentialsProvider, DB session strategy (`adapter: PrismaAdapter`), callbacks to inject `id` + `role` onto session\n    27→- `src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` — NextAuth route handler\n    28→- `src/middleware.ts` — protect all routes except `/login`, `/api/auth/*`, and `/api/v1/*` (API routes use their own auth); redirect unauthenticated users to `/login`\n    29→- `src/lib/validations/auth.ts` — loginSchema (email + password)\n    30→- `src/types/next-auth.d.ts` — extend Session type with `id` and `role`\n    31→- `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` — centered login form (email/password)\n    32→- `prisma/seed.ts` — seed landlord user (email: admin@example.com, password: admin123)\n    33→\n    34→**Files to modify:**\n    35→- `prisma/schema.prisma` — add `Session` and `Account` models required by NextAuth DB session strategy + PrismaAdapter\n    36→- `src/app/layout.tsx` — wrap with `SessionProvider` + `Toaster`\n    37→- `src/app/page.tsx` — redirect to `/dashboard`\n    38→- `package.json` — add `\"prisma\": { \"seed\": \"npx tsx prisma/seed.ts\" }`, add `tsx` and `@auth/prisma-adapter` devDependencies\n    39→- `.env.example` — document required env vars (DATABASE_URL, AUTH_SECRET, AUTH_URL)\n    40→\n    41→**Auth pattern — layered, not repeated:**\n    42→\n    43→1. **Middleware** (`src/middleware.ts`) — redirects unauthenticated requests to `/login` at the edge. This protects all `(dashboard)` routes without any per-page code.\n    44→2. **Dashboard layout** (`src/app/(dashboard)/layout.tsx`) — calls `auth()` once, fetches the session, and makes user info available to all child pages (via props or a context provider). Individual pages do **not** call `requireAuth()`.\n    45→3. **Server actions** (`src/lib/actions/*.ts`) — each action still calls `requireAuth()` at the top. Mutations must always re-verify auth independently of the UI.\n    46→4. **API routes** (`src/app/api/v1/...`) — use API key auth (see Phase 1.5), not session auth.\n    47→\n    48→```typescript\n    49→// src/lib/auth.ts — helper used by server actions only\n    50→export async function requireAuth() {\n    51→  const session = await auth()\n    52→  if (!session?.user?.id) redirect(\"/login\")\n    53→  return session\n    54→}\n    55→```\n    56→\n    57→---\n    58→\n    59→## Phase 1.5: REST API & Service Layer (S04)\n    60→\n    61→External services (payment providers, automation tools, other apps) integrate via a versioned REST API. Business logic is extracted into a shared service layer so both server actions and API routes stay thin.\n    62→\n    63→**Service layer — files to create:**\n    64→- `src/lib/services/properties.ts` — findAll, findById, create, update, delete (all accept `ownerId`, no auth logic)\n    65→- `src/lib/services/units.ts` — CRUD scoped through property ownership\n    66→- `src/lib/services/tenants.ts` — CRUD\n    67→- `src/lib/services/leases.ts` — CRUD + business rules (one active lease per unit, status syncs unit occupancy)\n    68→- `src/lib/services/charges.ts` — generateRentCharges, list\n    69→- `src/lib/services/payments.ts` — recordPayment with allocation logic\n    70→\n    71→> Service functions are pure business logic: they take validated data + `ownerId`, talk to Prisma, and return results. No `requireAuth()`, no `revalidatePath()`, no HTTP concerns. Server actions and API routes are thin wrappers that handle auth, validation, and response formatting.\n    72→\n    73→**API key auth:**\n    74→- `src/lib/api-auth.ts` — `requireApiKey(request)` helper that validates `Authorization: Bearer <key>` header against `API_KEY` env var. Returns 401 on failure. Future: per-user API keys stored in DB.\n    75→- `.env.example` — add `API_KEY` var\n    76→\n    77→**API routes — files to create:**\n    78→- `src/app/api/v1/properties/route.ts` — `GET` (list), `POST` (create)\n    79→- `src/app/api/v1/properties/[propertyId]/route.ts` — `GET`, `PUT`, `DELETE`\n    80→- `src/app/api/v1/properties/[propertyId]/units/route.ts` — `GET` (list), `POST` (create)\n    81→- `src/app/api/v1/properties/[propertyId]/units/[unitId]/route.ts` — `GET`, `PUT`, `DELETE`\n    82→- `src/app/api/v1/tenants/route.ts` — `GET`, `POST`\n    83→- `src/app/api/v1/tenants/[tenantId]/route.ts` — `GET`, `PUT`, `DELETE`\n    84→- `src/app/api/v1/leases/route.ts` — `GET`, `POST`\n    85→- `src/app/api/v1/leases/[leaseId]/route.ts` — `GET`, `PUT`, `DELETE`\n    86→- `src/app/api/v1/charges/route.ts` — `GET` (list with filters), `POST` (generate rent charges)\n    87→- `src/app/api/v1/payments/route.ts` — `GET`, `POST` (record payment / webhook target)\n    88→\n    89→**API conventions:**\n    90→- All responses: `{ data: T }` on success, `{ error: string, details?: object }` on failure\n    91→- Standard HTTP status codes: 200, 201, 400 (validation), 401, 404, 500\n    92→- Pagination: `?page=1&limit=20` query params, response includes `{ data, meta: { page, limit, total } }`\n    93→- Filtering: entity-specific query params (e.g., `?status=ACTIVE`, `?propertyId=...`)\n    94→\n    95→**Refactor existing server actions:**\n    96→- `src/lib/actions/properties.ts` — becomes a thin wrapper: calls `requireAuth()`, validates input, calls service, calls `revalidatePath()`\n    97→- Same pattern for all other action files\n    98→\n    99→---\n   100→\n   101→## Phase 2: Dashboard Layout & Shared Components\n   102→\n   103→**Files to create:**\n   104→- `src/app/(dashboard)/layout.tsx` — flex layout with sidebar + scrollable main content area\n   105→- `src/app/(dashboard)/page.tsx` — dashboard home with summary stat cards (properties, units, active leases, outstanding balance)\n   106→- `src/components/sidebar.tsx` — nav links (Dashboard, Properties, Tenants, Leases, Billing) with lucide icons, active state highlighting, sign-out button. **Mobile responsive**: uses `Sheet` component for hamburger menu on small screens\n   107→- `src/components/page-header.tsx` — reusable title + description + optional action button\n   108→- `src/components/breadcrumbs.tsx` — breadcrumb navigation generated from URL segments (e.g. Properties > 123 Main St > Edit)\n   109→- `src/components/empty-state.tsx` — icon + message + optional CTA for empty lists\n   110→- `src/components/status-badge.tsx` — colored badge for all status enums\n   111→- `src/components/delete-dialog.tsx` — confirmation AlertDialog wrapper\n   112→\n   113→**Loading skeletons** — create `loading.tsx` files for each route group:\n   114→- `src/app/(dashboard)/loading.tsx`\n   115→- `src/app/(dashboard)/properties/loading.tsx`\n   116→- `src/app/(dashboard)/tenants/loading.tsx`\n   117→- `src/app/(dashboard)/leases/loading.tsx`\n   118→- `src/app/(dashboard)/billing/loading.tsx`\n   119→\n   120→**Utilities to add to `src/lib/utils.ts`:**\n   121→- `getFullAddress()`, `getTenantFullName()`, `getOutstandingAmount()`\n   122→\n   123→---\n   124→\n   125→## Phase 3: Properties + Units CRUD (S05-S06)\n   126→\n   127→**Files to create:**\n   128→- `src/lib/validations/property.ts` — propertySchema (name, address, city, state, zipCode, notes)\n   129→- `src/lib/validations/unit.ts` — unitSchema (unitNumber, bedrooms, bathrooms, sqft, marketRent, status, notes)\n   130→- `src/lib/actions/properties.ts` — thin wrappers: `requireAuth()` → validate → call service → `revalidatePath()`\n   131→- `src/lib/actions/units.ts` — thin wrappers: same pattern, ownership verified via property relation in service layer\n   132→- `src/components/forms/property-form.tsx` — shared create/edit form (react-hook-form + zodResolver)\n   133→- `src/components/forms/unit-form.tsx` — shared create/edit unit form\n   134→- `src/app/(dashboard)/properties/page.tsx` — properties list table\n   135→- `src/app/(dashboard)/properties/new/page.tsx` — create property\n   136→- `src/app/(dashboard)/properties/[propertyId]/page.tsx` — property detail + inline units list\n   137→- `src/app/(dashboard)/properties/[propertyId]/edit/page.tsx` — edit property\n   138→- `src/app/(dashboard)/properties/[propertyId]/units/new/page.tsx` — add unit to property\n   139→- `src/app/(dashboard)/properties/[propertyId]/units/[unitId]/edit/page.tsx` — edit unit\n   140→\n   141→---\n   142→\n   143→## Phase 4: Tenants + Leases (S07-S08)\n   144→\n   145→**Files to create:**\n   146→- `src/lib/validations/tenant.ts` — tenantSchema (firstName, lastName, email, phone, notes)\n   147→- `src/lib/validations/lease.ts` — leaseSchema (tenantId, unitId, dates, rentAmount, securityDeposit, rentDueDay, status, notes) with refinement: endDate > startDate\n   148→- `src/lib/actions/tenants.ts` — thin wrappers calling tenant service\n   149→- `src/lib/actions/leases.ts` — thin wrappers calling lease service (business rules live in `src/lib/services/leases.ts`):\n   150→  - Only one ACTIVE lease per unit at a time\n   151→  - ACTIVE lease sets unit status to OCCUPIED\n   152→  - TERMINATED/EXPIRED sets unit to VACANT\n   153→- `src/lib/actions/uploads.ts` — file upload handler (write to `data/uploads/`, return filename)\n   154→- `src/app/api/uploads/[filename]/route.ts` — serve uploaded files with correct content-type\n   155→- `src/components/forms/tenant-form.tsx` — shared tenant form\n   156→- `src/components/forms/lease-form.tsx` — lease form with tenant/unit Select dropdowns, date pickers, file input for PDF\n   157→- `src/app/(dashboard)/tenants/page.tsx` — tenants list with active unit info\n   158→- `src/app/(dashboard)/tenants/new/page.tsx` — create tenant\n   159→- `src/app/(dashboard)/tenants/[tenantId]/page.tsx` — tenant detail (profile, active lease, balance, charges, payments)\n   160→- `src/app/(dashboard)/tenants/[tenantId]/edit/page.tsx` — edit tenant\n   161→- `src/app/(dashboard)/leases/page.tsx` — all leases list with status badges\n   162→- `src/app/(dashboard)/leases/new/page.tsx` — create lease\n   163→- `src/app/(dashboard)/leases/[leaseId]/page.tsx` — lease detail (charges table, payments)\n   164→\n   165→---\n   166→\n   167→## Phase 5: Billing — Charges + Payments (S09, S11)\n   168→\n   169→**Files to create:**\n   170→- `src/lib/validations/charge.ts` — generateChargesSchema (month, year)\n   171→- `src/lib/validations/payment.ts` — paymentSchema (tenantId, amount, method, receivedDate, reference, notes)\n   172→- `src/lib/actions/charges.ts` — thin wrapper calling charge service's `generateRentCharges(ownerId, month, year)`\n   173→- `src/lib/actions/payments.ts` — thin wrapper calling payment service's `recordPayment(ownerId, data)`\n   174→- `src/components/forms/payment-form.tsx` — payment form with tenant select, amount, method, date, reference\n   175→- `src/app/(dashboard)/billing/page.tsx` — outstanding charges overview, total balance, quick action buttons\n   176→- `src/app/(dashboard)/billing/charges/generate/page.tsx` — month/year picker to generate rent charges\n   177→- `src/app/(dashboard)/billing/payments/new/page.tsx` — record payment form\n   178→\n   179→---\n   180→\n   181→## Phase 6: Polish & Setup\n   182→\n   183→- Run initial Prisma migration (`npx prisma migrate dev --name init`)\n   184→- Run seed script (`npx prisma db seed`)\n   185→- Update `.gitignore` (add `data/uploads/*`, `src/generated/`, `.env`, `.env.local`)\n   186→- Create `.env.example`\n   187→- Output plan as `prd.md` at project root for Ralph to reference\n   188→- Smoke test all flows end-to-end\n   189→\n   190→---\n   191→\n   192→## Verification Plan\n   193→\n   194→1. Start Postgres: `docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d`\n   195→2. Run migration: `npx prisma migrate dev --name init`\n   196→3. Seed database: `npx prisma db seed`\n   197→4. Start dev server: `npm run dev`\n   198→5. Test auth: login with admin@example.com / admin123, verify redirect to dashboard\n   199→6. Test session revocation: logout, verify session is deleted from DB, verify protected pages redirect\n   200→7. Test properties: create property, add units, edit, delete\n   201→8. Test tenants: create tenant, verify list\n   202→9. Test leases: create lease linking tenant to unit, verify unit status changes to OCCUPIED\n   203→10. Test billing: generate rent charges for current month, verify charges appear\n   204→11. Test payments: record payment, verify it allocates to oldest charge, verify charge status updates\n   205→12. Test REST API: `curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $API_KEY\" http://localhost:3000/api/v1/properties` — verify JSON response\n   206→13. Test API create: POST to `/api/v1/tenants` with valid payload, verify 201 response\n   207→14. Test API auth: request without API key returns 401\n   208→\n   209→---\n   210→\n   211→## Notes\n   212→\n   213→- ~70 new files total (includes loading skeletons, breadcrumbs, mobile sidebar, service layer, API routes)\n   214→- **Multi-user from day one** — all queries scoped by `ownerId`, Tenant model has `userId` for future tenant portal access\n   215→- **DB sessions** — NextAuth PrismaAdapter with `Session` + `Account` models; supports instant revocation\n   216→- **Service layer** (`/src/lib/services/`) is the single source of business logic — server actions and API routes are thin wrappers\n   217→- **REST API** at `/api/v1/` with API key auth — enables external integrations, webhooks, and automation\n   218→- All monetary arithmetic uses `decimal.js` (never raw JS floats)\n   219→- Every server action starts with `requireAuth()` and scopes queries by `ownerId`; API routes use `requireApiKey()`\n   220→- Auth for pages is handled by middleware + dashboard layout — individual pages do not call `requireAuth()`\n   221→- Zod v4 is installed — need to verify `@hookform/resolvers` v5 compatibility (it should work)\n   222→- `tsx` devDependency needed for seed script runner\n   223→- `@auth/prisma-adapter` needed for DB session strategy\n   224→- Property photos (S05 mentions photos) are deferred — the generic `Document` model can handle them later\n   225→- Lease PDF upload included (S08) — files stored in `data/uploads/`, served via API route\n   226→- Mobile responsive sidebar using shadcn `Sheet` component (hamburger trigger)\n   227→- Breadcrumb navigation in dashboard header derived from URL path\n   228→- Skeleton loading states (`loading.tsx`) for each major route group\n   229→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e98f50e7-37b3-40b4-9edf-745fd1d4ccd5","uuid":"8c90e569-5e3c-4b0e-a217-d1148bba61e9","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Volumes/Secondary/workspace/tenant-portal/prd/prd.md","content":"# Property Manager MVP - Implementation Plan\n\n## Context\n\nBuilding a self-hosted, multi-user property management app. Landlords manage properties, units, leases, and billing; tenants can be linked to user accounts for future portal access. The project scaffolding (S01) and database schema (S02) are complete. We need to implement: authentication (S03), REST API (S04), properties + units CRUD (S05-S06), tenants + leases (S07-S08), and billing (S09, S11).\n\nThe codebase already has: Next.js 14 App Router, Prisma schema (11 models), 23 shadcn/ui components, React Hook Form + Zod v4, NextAuth v5 beta, bcryptjs, date-fns, decimal.js, and Docker setup.\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Decisions\n\n- **Server Actions** for form mutations — colocated with forms, less boilerplate. Shared business logic lives in `/src/lib/services/` so both server actions and API routes can reuse it\n- **REST API** (`/api/v1/...`) for external integrations — API key auth for service-to-service calls, supports webhooks (e.g., payment providers) and automation\n- **DB session strategy** (`strategy: \"database\"`) — supports instant session revocation (critical for multi-user: landlord disables tenant, password changes, etc.), ability to list/manage active sessions, and no token-size bloat. Requires `Session` + `Account` models in Prisma\n- **Route groups**: `(auth)` for login, `(dashboard)` for all protected pages with shared sidebar layout\n- **Validation schemas**: `/src/lib/validations/` — one file per entity, shared between client, server actions, and API routes\n- **Server actions**: `/src/lib/actions/` — one file per entity, all prefixed with `\"use server\"`\n- **Service layer**: `/src/lib/services/` — one file per entity, pure business logic (no auth checks), called by both server actions and API routes\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Auth (S03)\n\n**Files to create:**\n- `src/lib/auth.ts` — NextAuth config: CredentialsProvider, DB session strategy (`adapter: PrismaAdapter`), callbacks to inject `id` + `role` onto session\n- `src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` — NextAuth route handler\n- `src/middleware.ts` — protect all routes except `/login`, `/api/auth/*`, and `/api/v1/*` (API routes use their own auth); redirect unauthenticated users to `/login`\n- `src/lib/validations/auth.ts` — loginSchema (email + password)\n- `src/types/next-auth.d.ts` — extend Session type with `id` and `role`\n- `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` — centered login form (email/password)\n- `prisma/seed.ts` — seed landlord user (email: admin@example.com, password: admin123)\n\n**Files to modify:**\n- `prisma/schema.prisma` — add `Session` and `Account` models required by NextAuth DB session strategy + PrismaAdapter\n- `src/app/layout.tsx` — wrap with `SessionProvider` + `Toaster`\n- `src/app/page.tsx` — redirect to `/dashboard`\n- `package.json` — add `\"prisma\": { \"seed\": \"npx tsx prisma/seed.ts\" }`, add `tsx` and `@auth/prisma-adapter` devDependencies\n- `.env.example` — document required env vars (DATABASE_URL, AUTH_SECRET, AUTH_URL)\n\n**Auth pattern — layered, not repeated:**\n\n1. **Middleware** (`src/middleware.ts`) — redirects unauthenticated requests to `/login` at the edge. This protects all `(dashboard)` routes without any per-page code.\n2. **Dashboard layout** (`src/app/(dashboard)/layout.tsx`) — calls `auth()` once, fetches the session, and makes user info available to all child pages (via props or a context provider). Individual pages do **not** call `requireAuth()`.\n3. **Server actions** (`src/lib/actions/*.ts`) — each action still calls `requireAuth()` at the top. Mutations must always re-verify auth independently of the UI.\n4. **API routes** (`src/app/api/v1/...`) — use API key auth (see Phase 1.5), not session auth.\n\n```typescript\n// src/lib/auth.ts — helper used by server actions only\nexport async function requireAuth() {\n  const session = await auth()\n  if (!session?.user?.id) redirect(\"/login\")\n  return session\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1.5: REST API & Service Layer (S04)\n\nExternal services (payment providers, automation tools, other apps) integrate via a versioned REST API. Business logic is extracted into a shared service layer so both server actions and API routes stay thin.\n\n**Service layer — files to create:**\n- `src/lib/services/properties.ts` — findAll, findById, create, update, delete (all accept `ownerId`, no auth logic)\n- `src/lib/services/units.ts` — CRUD scoped through property ownership\n- `src/lib/services/tenants.ts` — CRUD\n- `src/lib/services/leases.ts` — CRUD + business rules (one active lease per unit, status syncs unit occupancy)\n- `src/lib/services/charges.ts` — generateRentCharges, list\n- `src/lib/services/payments.ts` — recordPayment with allocation logic\n\n> Service functions are pure business logic: they take validated data + `ownerId`, talk to Prisma, and return results. No `requireAuth()`, no `revalidatePath()`, no HTTP concerns. Server actions and API routes are thin wrappers that handle auth, validation, and response formatting.\n\n**API key auth:**\n- `src/lib/api-auth.ts` — `requireApiKey(request)` helper that validates `Authorization: Bearer <key>` header against `API_KEY` env var. Returns 401 on failure. Future: per-user API keys stored in DB.\n- `.env.example` — add `API_KEY` var\n\n**API routes — files to create:**\n- `src/app/api/v1/properties/route.ts` — `GET` (list), `POST` (create)\n- `src/app/api/v1/properties/[propertyId]/route.ts` — `GET`, `PUT`, `DELETE`\n- `src/app/api/v1/properties/[propertyId]/units/route.ts` — `GET` (list), `POST` (create)\n- `src/app/api/v1/properties/[propertyId]/units/[unitId]/route.ts` — `GET`, `PUT`, `DELETE`\n- `src/app/api/v1/tenants/route.ts` — `GET`, `POST`\n- `src/app/api/v1/tenants/[tenantId]/route.ts` — `GET`, `PUT`, `DELETE`\n- `src/app/api/v1/leases/route.ts` — `GET`, `POST`\n- `src/app/api/v1/leases/[leaseId]/route.ts` — `GET`, `PUT`, `DELETE`\n- `src/app/api/v1/charges/route.ts` — `GET` (list with filters), `POST` (generate rent charges)\n- `src/app/api/v1/payments/route.ts` — `GET`, `POST` (record payment / webhook target)\n\n**API conventions:**\n- All responses: `{ data: T }` on success, `{ error: string, details?: object }` on failure\n- Standard HTTP status codes: 200, 201, 400 (validation), 401, 404, 500\n- Pagination: `?page=1&limit=20` query params, response includes `{ data, meta: { page, limit, total } }`\n- Filtering: entity-specific query params (e.g., `?status=ACTIVE`, `?propertyId=...`)\n\n**Refactor existing server actions:**\n- `src/lib/actions/properties.ts` — becomes a thin wrapper: calls `requireAuth()`, validates input, calls service, calls `revalidatePath()`\n- Same pattern for all other action files\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Dashboard Layout & Shared Components\n\n**Files to create:**\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/layout.tsx` — flex layout with sidebar + scrollable main content area\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/page.tsx` — dashboard home with summary stat cards (properties, units, active leases, outstanding balance)\n- `src/components/sidebar.tsx` — nav links (Dashboard, Properties, Tenants, Leases, Billing) with lucide icons, active state highlighting, sign-out button. **Mobile responsive**: uses `Sheet` component for hamburger menu on small screens\n- `src/components/page-header.tsx` — reusable title + description + optional action button\n- `src/components/breadcrumbs.tsx` — breadcrumb navigation generated from URL segments (e.g. Properties > 123 Main St > Edit)\n- `src/components/empty-state.tsx` — icon + message + optional CTA for empty lists\n- `src/components/status-badge.tsx` — colored badge for all status enums\n- `src/components/delete-dialog.tsx` — confirmation AlertDialog wrapper\n\n**Loading skeletons** — create `loading.tsx` files for each route group:\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/loading.tsx`\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/properties/loading.tsx`\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/tenants/loading.tsx`\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/leases/loading.tsx`\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/billing/loading.tsx`\n\n**Utilities to add to `src/lib/utils.ts`:**\n- `getFullAddress()`, `getTenantFullName()`, `getOutstandingAmount()`\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Properties + Units CRUD (S05-S06)\n\n**Files to create:**\n- `src/lib/validations/property.ts` — propertySchema (name, address, city, state, zipCode, notes)\n- `src/lib/validations/unit.ts` — unitSchema (unitNumber, bedrooms, bathrooms, sqft, marketRent, status, notes)\n- `src/lib/actions/properties.ts` — thin wrappers: `requireAuth()` → validate → call service → `revalidatePath()`\n- `src/lib/actions/units.ts` — thin wrappers: same pattern, ownership verified via property relation in service layer\n- `src/components/forms/property-form.tsx` — shared create/edit form (react-hook-form + zodResolver)\n- `src/components/forms/unit-form.tsx` — shared create/edit unit form\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/properties/page.tsx` — properties list table\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/properties/new/page.tsx` — create property\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/properties/[propertyId]/page.tsx` — property detail + inline units list\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/properties/[propertyId]/edit/page.tsx` — edit property\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/properties/[propertyId]/units/new/page.tsx` — add unit to property\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/properties/[propertyId]/units/[unitId]/edit/page.tsx` — edit unit\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Tenants + Leases (S07-S08)\n\n**Files to create:**\n- `src/lib/validations/tenant.ts` — tenantSchema (firstName, lastName, email, phone, notes)\n- `src/lib/validations/lease.ts` — leaseSchema (tenantId, unitId, dates, rentAmount, securityDeposit, rentDueDay, status, notes) with refinement: endDate > startDate\n- `src/lib/actions/tenants.ts` — thin wrappers calling tenant service\n- `src/lib/actions/leases.ts` — thin wrappers calling lease service (business rules live in `src/lib/services/leases.ts`):\n  - Only one ACTIVE lease per unit at a time\n  - ACTIVE lease sets unit status to OCCUPIED\n  - TERMINATED/EXPIRED sets unit to VACANT\n- `src/lib/actions/uploads.ts` — file upload handler (write to `data/uploads/`, return filename)\n- `src/app/api/uploads/[filename]/route.ts` — serve uploaded files with correct content-type\n- `src/components/forms/tenant-form.tsx` — shared tenant form\n- `src/components/forms/lease-form.tsx` — lease form with tenant/unit Select dropdowns, date pickers, file input for PDF\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/tenants/page.tsx` — tenants list with active unit info\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/tenants/new/page.tsx` — create tenant\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/tenants/[tenantId]/page.tsx` — tenant detail (profile, active lease, balance, charges, payments)\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/tenants/[tenantId]/edit/page.tsx` — edit tenant\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/leases/page.tsx` — all leases list with status badges\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/leases/new/page.tsx` — create lease\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/leases/[leaseId]/page.tsx` — lease detail (charges table, payments)\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Billing — Charges + Payments (S09, S11)\n\n**Files to create:**\n- `src/lib/validations/charge.ts` — generateChargesSchema (month, year)\n- `src/lib/validations/payment.ts` — paymentSchema (tenantId, amount, method, receivedDate, reference, notes)\n- `src/lib/actions/charges.ts` — thin wrapper calling charge service's `generateRentCharges(ownerId, month, year)`\n- `src/lib/actions/payments.ts` — thin wrapper calling payment service's `recordPayment(ownerId, data)`\n- `src/components/forms/payment-form.tsx` — payment form with tenant select, amount, method, date, reference\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/billing/page.tsx` — outstanding charges overview, total balance, quick action buttons\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/billing/charges/generate/page.tsx` — month/year picker to generate rent charges\n- `src/app/(dashboard)/billing/payments/new/page.tsx` — record payment form\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Polish & Setup\n\n- Run initial Prisma migration (`npx prisma migrate dev --name init`)\n- Run seed script (`npx prisma db seed`)\n- Update `.gitignore` (add `data/uploads/*`, `src/generated/`, `.env`, `.env.local`)\n- Create `.env.example`\n- Output plan as `prd.md` at project root for Ralph to reference\n- Smoke test all flows end-to-end\n\n---\n\n## Verification Plan\n\n1. Start Postgres: `docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d`\n2. Run migration: `npx prisma migrate dev --name init`\n3. Seed database: `npx prisma db seed`\n4. Start dev server: `npm run dev`\n5. Test auth: login with admin@example.com / admin123, verify redirect to dashboard\n6. Test session revocation: logout, verify session is deleted from DB, verify protected pages redirect\n7. Test properties: create property, add units, edit, delete\n8. Test tenants: create tenant, verify list\n9. Test leases: create lease linking tenant to unit, verify unit status changes to OCCUPIED\n10. Test billing: generate rent charges for current month, verify charges appear\n11. Test payments: record payment, verify it allocates to oldest charge, verify charge status updates\n12. Test REST API: `curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $API_KEY\" http://localhost:3000/api/v1/properties` — verify JSON response\n13. Test API create: POST to `/api/v1/tenants` with valid payload, verify 201 response\n14. Test API auth: request without API key returns 401\n\n---\n\n## Notes\n\n- ~70 new files total (includes loading skeletons, breadcrumbs, mobile sidebar, service layer, API routes)\n- **Multi-user from day one** — all queries scoped by `ownerId`, Tenant model has `userId` for future tenant portal access\n- **DB sessions** — NextAuth PrismaAdapter with `Session` + `Account` models; supports instant revocation\n- **Service layer** (`/src/lib/services/`) is the single source of business logic — server actions and API routes are thin wrappers\n- **REST API** at `/api/v1/` with API key auth — enables external integrations, webhooks, and automation\n- All monetary arithmetic uses `decimal.js` (never raw JS floats)\n- Every server action starts with `requireAuth()` and scopes queries by `ownerId`; API routes use `requireApiKey()`\n- Auth for pages is handled by middleware + dashboard layout — individual pages do not call `requireAuth()`\n- Zod v4 is installed — need to verify `@hookform/resolvers` v5 compatibility (it should work)\n- `tsx` devDependency needed for seed script runner\n- `@auth/prisma-adapter` needed for DB session strategy\n- Property photos (S05 mentions photos) are deferred — the generic `Document` model can handle them later\n- Lease PDF upload included (S08) — files stored in `data/uploads/`, served via API route\n- Mobile responsive sidebar using shadcn `Sheet` component (hamburger trigger)\n- Breadcrumb navigation in dashboard header derived from URL path\n- Skeleton loading states (`loading.tsx`) for each major route group\n","numLines":229,"startLine":1,"totalLines":229}}}
